00:10:43.898 --> 00:10:48.163
What's a weakness that I
can't, God, I really...

00:10:48.855 --> 00:10:51.431
So first and foremost, the
answer to the question is

00:10:51.431 --> 00:10:53.439
there's no absolute here.

00:10:53.439 --> 00:10:55.378
This is more like 80,
20, where maybe I would

00:10:55.378 --> 00:10:57.955
switch it from an 80, 20 to a 20, 80.

00:10:57.955 --> 00:10:59.511
That's one of the first reactions I have.

00:10:59.511 --> 00:11:01.275
There's nothing I'd
be, there's no strength

00:11:01.275 --> 00:11:03.261
I wanna give up...

00:11:03.261 --> 00:11:05.815
So fast.

00:11:05.815 --> 00:11:09.884
You know at some level...

00:11:10.494 --> 00:11:12.350
(laughter)

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.511
Yeah, like you know,
I'm a little combative

00:11:14.511 --> 00:11:17.052
in meetings at times with clients where,

00:11:17.052 --> 00:11:19.234
like I love competition so much,

00:11:19.234 --> 00:11:21.069
I would say being competitive is probably

00:11:21.069 --> 00:11:23.885
as big of a deal as it
is, but I would say that

00:11:23.885 --> 00:11:27.634
my competition, competitive
gene goes five to seven percent

00:11:27.634 --> 00:11:30.270
too far, I would give up
five to seven percent of it

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:33.009
because it's insane, like you know,

00:11:33.009 --> 00:11:35.307
I mean you guys know
how I play basketball.

00:11:35.307 --> 00:11:38.047
Like I really am mad,
like I wanna hurt people,

00:11:38.047 --> 00:11:40.405
like I wanna hurt people's
feelings in meetings.

00:11:40.405 --> 00:11:43.278
(competitive banter)

00:11:47.788 --> 00:11:50.886
I literally, like in
meetings will turn red,

00:11:50.886 --> 00:11:53.243
my eyes will turn red when
somebody says something

00:11:53.243 --> 00:11:56.332
that I think is really
disrespectful to my company,

00:11:56.332 --> 00:11:59.744
and literally try to historically
clown them in the meeting

00:11:59.744 --> 00:12:03.529
so that forever their
contemporaries at that table,

00:12:03.529 --> 00:12:05.782
I literally want to say
things that the other people

00:12:05.782 --> 00:12:08.163
at the table on their side
tell to their grandchildren.

00:12:08.163 --> 00:12:09.563
Like, "Oh, I was once in this meeting with

00:12:09.563 --> 00:12:11.020
"this Gary Vaynerchuk guy and said that

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.237
"Rick was a douche bag
boss, he said fuck you."

00:12:13.237 --> 00:12:15.593
You know like I'm very into that.

00:12:15.593 --> 00:12:18.274
I wanna like end the debate in the room

00:12:18.274 --> 00:12:20.574
at that time, whereas I
could've done it afterwards,

00:12:20.574 --> 00:12:22.674
I could've done it a little
more politically correct.

00:12:22.674 --> 00:12:26.192
But if I get to that rogue
tilt place emotionally

00:12:26.192 --> 00:12:28.537
in a business meeting,
even maybe the first time

00:12:28.537 --> 00:12:31.092
we ever meet, 
I let my competitive juices,

00:12:31.092 --> 00:12:33.912
I can feel it, it's like that
Incredible Hulk type stuff.

00:12:33.912 --> 00:12:35.920
Like I can feel like, oh
crap, I'm about to destroy

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.534
